# Example: the sites to ADD to the vendor host's Caddyfile (OVH, /etc/caddy/Caddyfile) for each
# LAN-only center that wants its website, online booking and patient portal on the internet.
# Runbook: docs/runbooks/public-edge.md. Rules: ADR 0028 decisions 3, 5 and 6.
#
# Install once on the host:
#   sudo install -d /etc/caddy/hospital-edge/fallback
#   sudo install -m 0644 infra/edge/edge.caddy /etc/caddy/hospital-edge/edge.caddy
#   sudo install -m 0644 infra/edge/fallback/index.html /etc/caddy/hospital-edge/fallback/index.html
#
# Keep the existing sites of the host as they are. Do NOT add a global
# `servers { trusted_proxies ... }` to this host: the edge is the outermost proxy and must
# overwrite X-Forwarded-For with the visitor's address (decision 6).

# One block per center: its public name, its tunnel address and the HTTP port its compose `web`
# publishes, then the name and phone shown when the center cannot be reached.
center-one.example.sd {
	import /etc/caddy/hospital-edge/edge.caddy 10.213.0.2:80 /etc/caddy/hospital-edge/fallback "مركز المثال الطبي" "+249 900 000 000"
}

# A second center on its own tunnel address.
# center-two.example.sd {
# 	import /etc/caddy/hospital-edge/edge.caddy 10.213.0.3:80 /etc/caddy/hospital-edge/fallback "مركز آخر" "+249 900 000 001"
# }
